{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S5 — Signed verdicts stamp provider, endpoint, tier, and effective capabilities\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nA signed gate verdict records only a model string: `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py:601` and\n`src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py:206,223` each write `\"model\": verdict.get(\"model\")`. That string is the\nresolved `provider:model`, so a verdict produced behind an opaque gateway still claims it came from\n`anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`. Once rebar supports two first-class providers and a best-effort tier, a consumer\ncannot tell a Bedrock-backed verdict from an Ollama-backed one, even though rebar signs both.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep the existing `model` string field untouched and **add** a sibling `provider_provenance` object:\n`{provider, model, endpoint_host, tier, capabilities}`. `endpoint_host` records the host only (never a full URL,\nnever credentials); `tier` is `first_class` or `best_effort`; `capabilities` is the effective record from S2\n[rebar:f184-a5f1-f181-4700]. Verdicts still sign on every tier — a contributor running Ollama can still exercise\nthe gates, which matters for the OSS on-ramp — but a consumer now has the lever to reject an off-tier verdict.\n\nAdditive-only is deliberate: it makes this a **backward-compatible** payload change, so an older reader ignores\nthe new key and no store-compatibility capability gate or migration is required. Readers that want the\nprovenance treat its absence as \"unknown, legacy\".\n\n**Alternative rejected:** refusing to sign off-tier verdicts. It gives a stronger guarantee but breaks local\ndevelopment without a first-class provider key, which weakens exactly the contributor on-ramp\n`docs/plan-review-gate.md` depends on.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** replacing the `model` string with the structured object. That is a breaking payload\nchange requiring a compatibility gate and a migration for zero added information.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` — expose the provenance record from the factory.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — populate it alongside `ran_model`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py` (`:601`), `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py` (`:206,223`).\n- `docs/event-schema.md` — document the additive field.\n- `tests/unit/test_verdict_provenance.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nContract tier: the mechanism is a producer/consumer shape agreement across a signed, persisted payload, so the\ntest feeds a real runner result into the real sidecar writer and reads the persisted record back.\n\n- happy path: a Bedrock run persists `provider_provenance.tier == \"first_class\"` and `provider == \"bedrock\"`.\n- best-effort path: a run with `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL` persists `tier == \"best_effort\"` and the endpoint host.\n- collateral invariant: the pre-existing `model` string field is byte-identical to what it was before this\n  change, and the signature over the payload still verifies.\n- security oracle (negative control): given a `base_url` containing credentials\n  (`https://user:secret@host/v1`), the persisted `endpoint_host` is `host` and the persisted payload contains\n  neither `secret` nor the api_key anywhere.\n- backward compatibility: a sidecar payload written WITHOUT the new key still loads and verifies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a test asserts no credential material from `base_url` or `api_key` appears anywhere in the persisted\n      sidecar payload\n- [ ] a test asserts a legacy payload lacking `provider_provenance` still loads and its signature verifies\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `rebar review-plan` on a real ticket writes a sidecar whose `provider_provenance.tier` matches the\n      configured provider, shown in the ticket comment\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` documents the field as additive and optional"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785011287301946001,"uuid":"8b52c543-f5d1-4daf-bb55-8280e8e48e2d"}